$'@a2 t'
$'  \e[2mWho, where from, how I got here.\e[0m'
$''
$'@a1 0'
$'@a1 1'
$'@a1 2'
$'@a1 3'
$'@a1 4'
$'@a1 5'
$'@a1 6'
$'@a1 7'
$'@a1 8'
$''
$'  I\'m Pedro Veríssimo, a builder from São Gabriel, a town of about'
$'  60,000 people in the far south of Brazil. When something grabs my'
$'  attention, I go all the way, until there\'s something I can point to.'
$''
$'  \e[2mfrom  \e[0m  São Gabriel, RS, fifth generation of rice and cattle farmers'
$'  \e[2mroute \e[0m  São Gabriel → Porto Alegre (2024) → São Paulo (2026)'
$'  \e[2mnow   \e[0m  tech co-founder of Sincra · Link School of Business'
$'  \e[2mspeaks\e[0m  Portuguese, English (C2, self-taught by 16), Spanish'
$''
$'  In 2024 I moved to Porto Alegre on my own, in the middle of a school'
$'  year, because that was the only window I had. Most of what\'s on these'
$'  pages happened after that move.'
$''
$'@a4 t'
$'  \e[2mWhat I am building now.\e[0m'
$''
$'@a3 0'
$'@a3 1'
$'@a3 2'
$'@a3 3'
$'@a3 4'
$'@a3 5'
$'@a3 6'
$''
$'  \e[1m"Doctors shouldn\'t pay interest on money that\'s already theirs."\e[0m'
$''
$'  In Brazil a surgeon can wait months to be paid for an operation, and'
$'  the hospital often can\'t tell where that money is stuck: internal'
$'  audit, the insurer, a missing signature. Sincra rebuilds every'
$'  procedure\'s path from surgery to payout and predicts how much each'
$'  doctor will receive, when, and with what confidence.'
$''
$'  \e[38;2;79;127;255m01 connect\e[0m\e[2m  →  \e[0m\e[38;2;79;127;255m02 rebuild\e[0m\e[2m  →  \e[0m\e[38;2;79;127;255m03 predict\e[0m\e[2m  →  \e[0m\e[38;2;79;127;255m04 show\e[0m\e[2m  →  \e[0m\e[38;2;79;127;255m05 advance\e[0m'
$''
$'  \e[2mrole   \e[0m  tech co-founder, one of three: product and engineering'
$'  \e[2mhistory\e[0m  started as shift scheduling; changed thesis at Link\'s Startup'
$'           School'
$'  \e[2mweb    \e[0m  https://sincra.app'
$''
$'@a6 t'
$'  \e[2mBuilt from fireworks up. São Gabriel, 2022–2023.\e[0m'
$''
$'@a0 0'
$'@a0 1'
$'@a0 2'
$'@a0 3'
$'@a0 4'
$'@a0 5'
$'@a0 6'
$'@a0 7'
$'@a0 8'
$'@a0 9'
$'@a0 10'
$'@a0 11'
$'@a0 12'
$'@a0 13'
$'@a0 14'
$'@a0 15'
$'@a0 16'
$'@a0 17'
$''
$'  No lab, no club, no budget: YouTube (BPS.space did most of the'
$'  teaching) and a lot of launches that didn\'t go to plan. I started by'
$'  taking fireworks apart and mounting them in cardboard tubes. The first'
$'  ones exploded; after enough iterations they flew.'
$''
$'  \e[38;2;255;106;46m▸\e[0m Home-mixed solid propellant, and a static fire on a kitchen scale'
$'    to read thrust.'
$'  \e[38;2;255;106;46m▸\e[0m An Arduino flight computer reading an accelerometer and driving'
$'    servos.'
$'  \e[38;2;255;106;46m▸\e[0m Parachute recovery, and cameras on board to film each flight.'
$'  \e[38;2;255;106;46m▸\e[0m Five rockets built. One pad fire. One flew in a corkscrew. I kept'
$'    every clip.'
$''
$'  \e[2mfilm\e[0m  Foguete 7/2023, the documentary: https://youtu.be/FnTpVjeVxYo'
$''
$'@a8 t'
$'  \e[2mGold at the 1st National AI Olympiad (ONIA), 2025.\e[0m'
$''
$'@a7 0'
$'@a7 1'
$'@a7 2'
$'@a7 3'
$'@a7 4'
$'@a7 5'
$'@a7 6'
$'@a7 7'
$''
$'  \e[38;2;46;230;166m\e[1m716,000+\e[0m\e[0m\e[2m participants   \e[0m\e[38;2;46;230;166m\e[1m28\e[0m\e[0m\e[2m golds   \e[0m\e[38;2;46;230;166m\e[1m1\e[0m\e[0m\e[2m of them mine\e[0m'
$''
$'  The rounds went from theory and ethics, to building models in Python,'
$'  to a final where I built a computer-vision algorithm for competing'
$'  robots, trained on Santos Dumont II, Brazil\'s national supercomputer.'
$''
$'  \e[2m┌─ rn.py · my submission ────────────────────────────────────────────┐\e[0m'
$'  \e[2m│ \e[0m\e[38;2;46;230;166mfrom sklearn.neural_network import MLPClassifier\e[0m'
$'  \e[2m│ \e[0m\e[38;2;46;230;166mfrom sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\e[0m'
$'  \e[2m│ \e[0m\e[38;2;46;230;166mimport pandas as pd\e[0m'
$'  \e[2m│ \e[0m\e[38;2;46;230;166m\e[0m'
$'  \e[2m│ \e[0m\e[38;2;46;230;166mtrain = pd.read_csv(\'treino.csv\')\e[0m'
$'  \e[2m│ \e[0m\e[38;2;46;230;166mX, y = train.drop([\'id\', \'target\'], axis=1), train[\'target\']\e[0m'
$'  \e[2m│ \e[0m\e[38;2;46;230;166mscaler = StandardScaler()\e[0m'
$'  \e[2m│ \e[0m\e[38;2;46;230;166mmodel = MLPClassifier(hidden_layer_sizes=(200), max_iter=1000,\e[0m'
$'  \e[2m│ \e[0m\e[38;2;46;230;166m                      random_state=42)\e[0m'
$'  \e[2m│ \e[0m\e[38;2;46;230;166mmodel.fit(scaler.fit_transform(X), y)\e[0m'
$'  \e[2m│ \e[0m\e[38;2;46;230;166m# what was missing, rounds later: save a checkpoint between jobs\e[0m'
$'  \e[2m└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\e[0m'
$''
$'  The one that got away: the selection for the international team'
$'  trained on jobs capped at 15 minutes. I never saved a checkpoint, so'
$'  every job started from zero. My model stalled near 70% when it could'
$'  have reached about 95%. One missing line of code between me and'
$'  Beijing.'
$''
$'  \e[2mcode \e[0m  https://github.com/peddrof/ONIA-Project'
$'  \e[2mafter\e[0m  named ambassador for the 2026 edition'
$''
$'@a10 t'
$'  \e[2mVolunteers meet NGOs. Porto Alegre, 2024–2025.\e[0m'
$''
$'@a9 0'
$'@a9 1'
$'@a9 2'
$'@a9 3'
$'@a9 4'
$'@a9 5'
$'@a9 6'
$'@a9 7'
$''
$'  At InovaTec, my school\'s student innovation club, I found lots of'
$'  ambition and almost no one who could build. As head of technology I'
$'  rebuilt the platform from scratch, and a team of four launched it in'
$'  about four months.'
$''
$'  \e[38;2;255;212;59m\e[1m170+\e[0m\e[0m\e[2m volunteers   \e[0m\e[38;2;255;212;59m\e[1m20\e[0m\e[0m\e[2m NGOs   \e[0m\e[38;2;255;212;59m\e[1m80+\e[0m\e[0m\e[2m blood donors   \e[0m\e[38;2;255;212;59m\e[1mR$6,300\e[0m\e[0m\e[2m Braille printer\e[0m'
$''
$'  Covered by RBS TV, SBT, Zero Hora, Brasil de Fato and Correio do Povo.'
$'  In July 2026 the students I trained used it to help fund an art school'
$'  in Morro da Cruz.'
$''
$'  \e[2mweb\e[0m  https://voluntariamais.com.br'
$''
$'@a12 t'
$'  \e[2mThree Instagram pages, 316,000 followers. All sold.\e[0m'
$''
$'@a11 0'
$'@a11 1'
$'@a11 2'
$'@a11 3'
$'@a11 4'
$'@a11 5'
$'@a11 6'
$'@a11 7'
$''
$'  My feed kept serving the same repeatable formats with millions of'
$'  views, so I tried to reverse-engineer them. The first two pages went'
$'  nowhere. Then a crab took off.'
$''
$'  \e[38;2;255;79;139m@seusiriqueijo\e[0m  183K  the most famous crab in Brazil'
$'  \e[38;2;255;79;139m@gatinhoajude \e[0m   83K  a cat drinking water; one reel: 340,088 accounts'
$'  \e[38;2;255;79;139m@inteligenciai\e[0m   50K  about AI'
$''
$'  7.2 million accounts reached in one 30-day window. My benchmark: the'
$'  two biggest accounts that started copying me. I couldn\'t monetize, so'
$'  I sold all three, for R$1,200, R$800 and R$160. Lesson: sell before'
$'  you build.'
$''
$'@a14 t'
$'  \e[2mA forecast that won, and a talk in Brasília. 2025.\e[0m'
$''
$'@a13 0'
$'@a13 1'
$'@a13 2'
$'@a13 3'
$'@a13 4'
$'@a13 5'
$'@a13 6'
$'@a13 7'
$''
$'  \e[38;2;79;127;255m\e[1mGERAÇÃO CALDEIRA\e[0m\e[0m \e[2m─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\e[0m'
$''
$'  200 selected from about 18,000. Our final project, a predictive sales'
$'  panel for RBS Group\'s fourth quarter, won. I turned down an internship'
$'  offer to keep building.'
$''
$'  \e[38;2;79;127;255m\e[1mII BRICS FORUM\e[0m\e[0m \e[2m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\e[0m'
$''
$'  Twenty minutes in Brasília, for diplomats and young leaders: "The'
$'  Youth Perspective: innovation starts small."'
$''
$'@a16 t'
$'  \e[2mFrom a cardboard cockpit to the real one.\e[0m'
$''
$'@a15 0'
$'@a15 1'
$'@a15 2'
$'@a15 3'
$'@a15 4'
$'@a15 5'
$'@a15 6'
$'@a15 7'
$''
$'  As a kid I built near full-scale cockpits out of cardboard, every'
$'  instrument drawn by hand. In May 2024, during the floods, with the'
$'  roads closed and a family emergency in Porto Alegre, I flew in as'
$'  co-pilot on a small plane found through a friend of a friend.'
$''
$'  \e[2msince\e[0m  ANAC private pilot ground school done · 10 hours flown'
$''
$'@a18 t'
$'  \e[2mSmaller things, each one finished.\e[0m'
$''
$'@a17 0'
$'@a17 1'
$'@a17 2'
$'@a17 3'
$'@a17 4'
$'@a17 5'
$'@a17 6'
$'@a17 7'
$'@a17 8'
$''
$'  \e[38;2;255;79;139m▸\e[0m Markets, age 12 (2020): the pandemic, a stock chart, and advice'
$'    nobody asked for. In 2026, presenting at B3 with my Link class.'
$'  \e[38;2;255;79;139m▸\e[0m Popsicles, age 14: sold at school until the principal banned it'
$'    for "causing disorder". Moved to the sidewalk at pickup time.'
$'    R$2,000 in a few months.'
$'  \e[38;2;255;79;139m▸\e[0m Step Up (2025): an NGO teaching English to low-income students. 32'
$'    lessons as a mentor, then operations and the tracking system.'
$'    stepuplearning.com.br'
$'  \e[38;2;255;79;139m▸\e[0m Advogado Rural: a publishing platform for a rural lawyer, so he'
$'    reaches farmers directly. advogadorural.com'
$'  \e[38;2;255;79;139m▸\e[0m Farroupilha AI: an essay-grading assistant for my school, OCR plus'
$'    a language model.'
$''
$'@a20 t'
$'  \e[2mFive generations of rice and cattle.\e[0m'
$''
$'@a19 0'
$'@a19 1'
$'@a19 2'
$'@a19 3'
$'@a19 4'
$'@a19 5'
$'@a19 6'
$'@a19 7'
$''
$'  My family has worked the land in Rio Grande do Sul for five'
$'  generations. When I\'m home I\'m in the corral for the vaccinations and'
$'  on the combine for the harvest.'
$''
$'@a22 t'
$'  \e[2mNine, in one list.\e[0m'
$''
